        // holds, the air slammed shut a tenth of a second later, then thunder going off
        // long and low from both sides. While it is gone (3 s), the loop heard along its
        // path: far-off thunder and a jet's roar going over high up, the sub breathing
        // under it, swelling toward the mark (`audio/warp.rs`; the rest of the battle is
        // held down under it). The arrival, the last second at the landing spot: the roar
        // diving in, growing and rising, the pressure building very low, crackle running
        // together, all stopping dead as it lands. The landing, heard over the whole map:
        // a crack, a huge slam and a sub thump that hits at once and holds for seconds, a
        // growl driven hard, crackle spitting all round and thinning, thunder rolling off
        // for three seconds with the ground slapping it back. The wave (its weapon's fire,
