        // The Springald's Triune Pinch-fusion Howitzer, heard 4 s before its shot: three
        // knots of fusion pinched into one. Three heavy clunks, left, middle and right, as
        // its blades unlock and draw back off the bore, grinding; then three rough low hums,
        // one from each lens, a little apart in pitch so they beat against each other in a
        // slow thrum. Over the last second and a half the pinch takes them: the three glide
        // together onto one note and the beating slows to stillness, air is drawn in down
        // the bore, its band falling, and a deep swell gathers under it. Crackle between the
        // knots comes and goes. Nothing climbs to a whine. It stops dead for the shot.
